		<conclusions GUID="_d5d2d1e2-b4dd-4157-b4a7-3dfae84e2845" eId="backCover">
			<?DMS-Component componentId="b627a471-567b-45de-80c9-370ba85cbdb3" seriesId="30145ec7-5249-4d20-b2a1-6828e1f3761f" versionNumber="1"?>
			<blockContainer GUID="_7ed65c59-31c8-4176-aaf8-183425abbe04" class="explanatoryNote" eId="backCover__explNote">
				<heading GUID="_3a037c6b-d07b-4aca-996f-1a3be459ff60" eId="backCover__explNote__hdg">Explanatory Note</heading>
				<subheading GUID="_9567ca32-6b46-49eb-9369-c1ce95c0da49" eId="backCover__explNote__subhdg">(This note is not part of the <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType"/>)</subheading>
				<p>These Regulations amend the Immigration and Nationality (Fees) Regulations 2018 (S.I. 2018/330) which set fees for the exercise of various functions in connection with immigration and nationality.</p>
				<p>Regulation 3 provides, by amendment, for a fee for victims of domestic abuse who wish to apply from overseas for indefinite leave to enter the United Kingdom. This is a fee for a new application which was not previously available. It also provides for waivers of those fees where the applicant satisfies a destitution test.</p>
				<p>Regulation 4 amends entry 9.3 in Schedule 2 to reflect the new Appendix Victim of Domestic Abuse to the immigration rules. It also amends entry 9.8 to reflect the new Appendix Statelessness, and further provides a fee exception for Part 14 applications under the immigration rules.</p>
				<p>A full impact assessment has not been prepared for this instrument as no, or no significant, impact on the private, voluntary or public sector is foreseen.</p>
			</blockContainer>
		</conclusions>
	</act>
